Ummm, you're not looking at the issue in its social
context, or in its "long term play" context.

Your figure _also_ says, in that former context,
that in any group of 1250 NetHack players, most
likely that chance just happened to one of them. In
a group as large as the readership of rgrn, it just
happened to several of us, at least in an abstract
sense, whether in a concrete sense we did or did not
reach Oracle, or did or did not break open the
statues to confirm the case.

So, _seeing such a posting here_ isn't "highly
unlikely" at all, in a social context. Being the
individual to whom the event just occurred follows
the odds as you stated them, _in one isolated set of
five games_. But there's a larger "among all my
games" context as well.

In my case, with about 680 games in my current
logfile, there are 675 places such a string of five
games in a row could have ended, so my chance of
having had the described event happen to me
(ignoring my odds of reaching Oracle at all, just in
"games in the abstract") somewhere within this set
of logfiled games is around 54::46.

Thus, running into this situation somewhere in a
long lifetime of NetHack play is "no surprise at
all". You're answer is correct, just incomplete.

And to bring closure, HJC panics too easily about
every little unusual happening. NetHack play is
_rife_ with unusual happenings, so unless they are
separately interesting they are better kept close
held than posted.

